attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a spine.** Columns 0 to 10, `ybjM` to `gstB`, are carried by 91 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 26% of calls {S1}. The model names 70 to 99% of them, fewest at column 2, `rcdA`, 70% {S1}.

@variable **A single variable column breaks the first spine**: column 11, `yliI`, carried by 88%, the most plastic stretch of the window {S2, P}. Then columns 16 to 19, `gsiD` to `gsiA`, are [[glutathione transport]] {S5, Q}. A second branch of 10 families runs through columns 36 to 45, share 15 to 26%, all shell {S8.b36}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 94 against 90%, and hesitates less there, 0.38 against 0.44 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 11, `yliI`, is a variable column, at 1.29 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in variable columns.** Columns 54 to 78, `cecR` to `ybhC`, are carried by 26 to 70% of chromosomes {S8.c54-78}. The last column is `ybhJ`, in 21% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 92% of genes**, 0.42 bits on average, perplexity 1.5 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.46 against 0.20 bits, and names fewer genes, 73% against 96% {C}.

